  "summary": "Bind current Shop evidence to its compiler while preserving historical receipts.",
  "why": "Luis approved the Pareto Shop evidence cleanup. Baseline: 216 passed, six stale receipt comparisons failed. RED f65a5ec: eleven failing guards. GREEN 8d88e49 binds complete compiler artifacts, including revision targets, and all output bytes to a separate evidence generation. Ten predecessor files and both graphs remain exact; no output field is ignored. Six historical Shop tests pass at the original producer in a clean local checkout. Expanded compiler/Shop/action/KG selection: 1054 passed, no skips. Final fourteen guards passed separately after one extra guard and a serialization refinement, not as a disjoint total. Final Shop plus fresh import: 236 passed, no skips. Ledger/current-byte guards: 2 passed. The fresh 106-event two-action log matches its prior proof exactly. No runtime, ontology, source, package, dependency, action-profile, paper, consumer or frozen-gate change. Effects remain synthetic; no full-repository, release or push claim.",
